# Hardhat + Local Auction Backend Setup

This guide explains how to:

- Run a local Ethereum blockchain (Hardhat)
- Deploy and interact with the contract
- Set up the Python backend environment
- Test the auction backend locally

------------------------------------------------------------
1Install Node.js (Required for Hardhat)
------------------------------------------------------------

Hardhat requires Node.js 20+.

curl -fsSL https://deb.nodesource.com/setup_22.x | sudo -E bash -
sudo apt-get install -y nodejs

Verify installation:
node -v


------------------------------------------------------------
 Install Project Dependencies
------------------------------------------------------------

From the project root (where package.json exists):

npm install


------------------------------------------------------------
3Start Local Blockchain
------------------------------------------------------------

Run:

npx hardhat node

This will:
- Start a JSON-RPC server at http://127.0.0.1:8545
- Generate 20 unlocked test accounts
- Fund each account with 10,000 ETH

IMPORTANT:
Leave this terminal running.


------------------------------------------------------------
 Deploy Contract to Local Node
------------------------------------------------------------

In a second terminal:

npx hardhat compile
npx hardhat run scripts/deploy.js --network localhost

This will output:

Contract deployed to: 0x...

Copy this address and update it in:

backend/mainauction.py


------------------------------------------------------------
 (Optional) Use Hardhat Console
------------------------------------------------------------

npx hardhat console --network localhost

Inside console:

const { ethers } = await import("ethers")
const provider = new ethers.JsonRpcProvider("http://127.0.0.1:8545")

Get accounts:
await provider.send("eth_accounts", [])


============================================================
PYTHON BACKEND SETUP
============================================================

------------------------------------------------------------
 Install Python & Tools
------------------------------------------------------------

sudo apt install -y python3 python3-pip python3-venv

python3 --version
pip3 --version


------------------------------------------------------------
 Create Virtual Environment
------------------------------------------------------------

From project root:

python3 -m venv venv

Activate it:

source venv/bin/activate


------------------------------------------------------------
 Install Python Dependencies
------------------------------------------------------------

pip install web3
pip install flask


------------------------------------------------------------
 Run Backend / Test Script
------------------------------------------------------------

Example test:

python test_mainauction.py

Or run Flask app:

python FLASKTEST.py


============================================================
DEVELOPMENT WORKFLOW
============================================================

Terminal 1:
npx hardhat node

Terminal 2:
npx hardhat compile
npx hardhat run scripts/deploy.js --network localhost

Terminal 3:
source venv/bin/activate
python test_mainauction.py


============================================================
IMPORTANT NOTES
============================================================

- Restarting "npx hardhat node" resets the blockchain state.
- You must redeploy the contract after restarting.
- Update the contract address in backend/mainauction.py after redeploy.
- Python backend assumes unlocked Hardhat accounts (default in Hardhat).
- Flask layer is optional for backend testing.


============================================================
SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE OVERVIEW
============================================================

Flask (HTTP Layer)
        ↓
mainauction.py (Controller Layer)
        ↓
bidding.py (Write Remote)
state.py   (Read Remote)
        ↓
Hardhat Local Blockchain (Ethereum Node)

Each layer can be tested independently.



